-- title:
--   Theorem 2.3 — two random matrices generate $\mathrm M(n,q)$ with probability $1-q^{-\Omega(n)}$
-- statement:
--   There are absolute constants $c>0$ and $n_0$ such that for every finite field $\mathbb F_q$ and every $n\ge n_0$, two independent uniformly random matrices $A_1,A_2\in\mathrm M(n,q)$ generate the full matrix algebra $\mathrm M(n,q)$ with probability at least $1-q^{-cn}$:
--   $$
--   \varepsilon_{\mathrm{gen}}(n,q)=\Pr\bigl[\mathbb F_q\langle A_1,A_2\rangle\neq\mathrm M(n,q)\bigr]\le q^{-cn}.
--   $$
--
--   The paper cites this from Neumann and Praeger [NP95, Theorem 6.1]. It shows that a generic pair of matrices has only scalar common centralizer, which is how the algorithm of Theorem 1.1 pins an isomorphism down to a scalar.
--
--   **Formalization Note** "Generate" is the unital subalgebra generated by $A_1,A_2$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--
--   - reading: probability 1 − 1/q^{Ω(n)} → ∃ c > 0, n₀ before the field, failure ≤ q^{−cn} for n ≥ n₀; reason: Ω with an absolute constant, uniform in q (the stronger reading, paper.md R7)
--   - encoding: "generate the full matrix algebra" → `Algebra.adjoin K {A₁, A₂} = ⊤`; reason: the unital subalgebra; the proof of Corollary 2.4 uses that its centralizer is the scalars
-- source:
--   Li, Li, Qiao, Tao, Wang, On the average-case complexity landscape for Tensor-Isomorphism-complete problems over finite fields, arXiv:2604.00591 (held version sha256 baf552e1…), Theorem 2.3, p.15 (PDF p.17)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AvgCaseTI_epsGen

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

namespace AvgCaseTI

/-- **Theorem 2.3 (Neumann–Praeger: two random matrices generate `M(n, q)`).**

Li, Li, Qiao, Tao, Wang, arXiv:2604.00591 (held version sha256 baf552e1…), Theorem 2.3, p.15
(PDF p.17), citing [NP95, Theorem 6.1]: "Let A₁, A₂ ∈ M(n, q) be two independent uniformly random
matrices. Then A₁ and A₂ generate the full matrix algebra M(n, q) with probability 1 − 1/q^{Ω(n)}."

There are absolute constants `c > 0` and `n₀` such that for every finite field and every `n ≥ n₀`,
`ε_gen(n, q) = Pr[A₁, A₂ do not generate M(n, q)] ≤ q^{−cn}`.

**Formalization Note.** `Ω(n)` is read uniformly in `q` (constants before the field). "Generate" is
the unital subalgebra (`Algebra.adjoin`). -/
theorem theorem_2_3 :
    ∃ c : ℝ, 0 < c ∧ ∃ n₀ : ℕ, ∀ (K : Type u) [Field K] [Fintype K], ∀ n : ℕ, n₀ ≤ n →
      epsGen K n ≤ (Fintype.card K : ℝ) ^ (-(c * n)) := by sorry

end AvgCaseTI
